# {{.Slug}}

Automated PR review. Listens for GitHub `pull_request` webhooks (action
= opened), fetches the diff, asks an LLM endpoint for a review, posts
the response as a PR comment.

Generated by `reactor new github-pr-reviewer {{.Slug}}` on {{.Date}}.

## Prerequisites

Two vault credentials:

```bash
reactor vault add --name github-pat --provider shared-secret --value $GITHUB_PAT
reactor vault add --name llm-api-key --provider shared-secret --value $LLM_BEARER
reactor vault grant --workflow {{.Slug}} --credential github-pat
reactor vault grant --workflow {{.Slug}} --credential llm-api-key
```

The GitHub PAT needs `repo:status` + `pull_requests:write`. Set the
LLM endpoint URL inside `main.go` (currently a placeholder).

## Set up the webhook

In the dashboard at `/workflows/{{.Slug}}` click "Add webhook trigger"
with provider `github`. The redirect flashes the URL + secret one time;
paste both into your repo's webhook config (Settings -> Webhooks ->
content type `application/json` + select `pull_request` events).

## Extend

Add review heuristics inline (file count, line count, CI status) before
the LLM step, or branch on `ev.PullRequest.Draft` to skip drafts.
